      "text": [
        " تَعَالَى إِنَّكُمْ لَفِي قَوْلٍ مُخْتَلِفٍ فِي أَمْرِ الْوَلَايَةِ يُؤْفَكُ عَنْهُ مَنْ أُفِكَ قَالَ مَنْ أُفِكَ عَنِ الْوَلَايَةِ أُفِكَ عَنِ الْجَنَّةِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Al Hassan Bin Sayf, from his brother, from his father, from Abu Hamza, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> regarding the Words of the Exalted <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:51#h8\"><a href=\"/books/quran:51#h8\">[51:8]</a></a> Most surely you are at variance with each other in what you say </span>regarding the matter of Al-Wilayah<span class=\"ibTxt\"> <a href=\"/#/books/quran:51#h9\"><a href=\"/books/quran:51#h9\">[51:9]</a></a> He is turned away from it who would be turned away</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The one who turns away from Al-Wilayah, turns away from the Paradise’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 48. Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad has narrated from Mu‘alla ibn Muhammad from Muhammad ibn Jumhur from Yunus who has said the following “A person in a marfu‘ narrated to me from abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.) about the words of Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most Gracious. “Yet, he has not entered into Aqaba <a href=\"/#/books/quran:90#h11\"><a href=\"/books/quran:90#h11\">[90:11]</a></a>. Would that you knew what Aqaba is! <a href=\"/#/books/quran:90#h12\"><a href=\"/books/quran:90#h12\">[90:12]</a></a>. It is the setting free of a slave.” <a href=\"/#/books/quran:90#h13\"><a href=\"/books/quran:90#h13\">[90:13]</a></a> The Imam (a.s.) said, “Setting free of a slave is acknowledgment of the Wilaya of Amir al-Mu’minin (a.s.), Leadership with Divine Authority.”"
        ]
      }
    },
